# Cataclysm 0.8 corrective implementation

Status: implemented locally; **NOT accepted for publication**. Independent mobile Chromium QA could not launch in this sandbox. No deployment, live-byte verification, physical-phone test, or independent QA approval is claimed.

## Scope and identity

Read `artifacts/mobile/job.json`, `plan.json` (selected IDs designer, researcher, engineer), `feedback.md` (empty array), current preview source and `game_factory/CATACLYSM_1_0_ROADMAP.md`. No gate.log existed. Edited only preview index.html, game.js, game.css and this report. Public/runtime/boot version remains 0.8; technical identifier and asset queries are `42500992714-1-correction`; diagnostics expose `patch`. Title now includes Cataclysm 0.8. BUILD_INFO release metadata was not edited because it is outside the allowed files: the runner must stamp it before publishing. Frozen 0.7, other games, dashboard, publishing code, dependencies and tests remain untouched. Existing repository history/base manifest supplies rollback provenance; no release commit or remote publication was created.

## Corrective blockers

- Root cause: offerUpgrade displayed every eligible button, including capped/disabled options, in an absolute dialog bounded by an overflow-hidden arena. Fourteen button heights exceed a phone arena; an arena scroll fix alone did not reduce complexity or eliminate dead choices. The dialog now uses viewport-fixed bounds, independent scrolling, three valid enabled choices, a guaranteed recover choice, and rotating access to the eligible upgrade pool. Choices have at least 68px height. Input capture and held keys are cleared entering/leaving selection; first choice receives focus. chooseUpgrade validates actual offered IDs, consumes pendingUpgrade once and returns to running. Existing queued XP resolution provides consecutive menus. No layout/touch usability claim is made without the blocked browser tests.
- Former damage 3 -> repeatable +0.25; speed +108 -> diminishing positive growth with logarithmic movement conversion; cooldown floor .24s -> repeatable ×.85 with excess attacks aggregated into damage at a .04s simulation volley floor. HP 6 -> unbounded milestone hearts and recovery also grants .25 max HP. Spread/ricochet/magnet rank 2 and combined special budget 4 -> removed. Familiar rank 3/pet pick limits -> removed; repeated familiar training increases weapon strength and lifetime. Beacon charges bank without stock cap; two active zones and one familiar remain simultaneous-entity limits. Familiar options remain offered when a familiar is already active.
- Performance controls: 95 enemies, 160 shots including familiar shots, at most nine spread projectiles, eight simulated bounces, two-second initial bullet lifetime. Extra spread, bounce ranks and firing frequency increase hit damage. Existing fish merging, bounded trails, pickup effects and reduced-motion particles retained. Movement grows with diminishing returns; enemy adaptation no longer scales linearly forever with player speed. Extremely large numerical values eventually meet floating-point limits; mathematical infinity is not supported.
- Time gates replace level/night archetype shortcuts: shambler 0s, weaver 120s, dasher 240s, orbiter 420s, stalker 660s, ghost 960s, gas 1200s. All unlocked regular archetypes remain in a deterministic rotating spawn pool. Nights now span 90s, letting familiar threats evolve before new introductions. Bosses stage every 300 simulation seconds; gas warns before damage and repeats every 30s after unlock. Player level cannot unlock archetypes, gas or bosses. Help/upgrade descriptions were rewritten to match these rules; obsolete cap notices removed.

## Selected playable features and interfaces

**designer — Survival Instinct Adrenaline Buff:** game.buffs.survivalInstinct is an eight-second duration. survivalTimer accrues twenty seconds only when not invulnerable, at least ten seconds since damage, and not already surged. First undamaged run may surge at 20s. Both contact and gas damage reset timer and cancel the buff. updateSupport multiplies speed by 1.15 and firing rate by 1.2. Rendered gold ring is static under reduced motion; activation has a unique adrenaline notification ID and synthesized cue. Used readable “+15% speed · +20% fire” text instead of the proposal's corrupt control character.

**researcher — Feral Instinct Overdrive:** edgeAid records the shield origin and starts game.escapeOverdriveTimer at 4.5s: the existing 2.5s shield plus the intended two-second escape window. This reconciles the otherwise impossible proposal of a two-second timer requiring a 2.5s shield to end first. After shield expiry, movement beyond 80px and no living enemy within 180px grants four seconds of game.feralInstinctOverdrive. It multiplies speed by 1.45 and damage by 1.6, exceeding base Feral's 1.3/1.25. Pink ring and distinct overdrive notification/sound signal activation. Timers expire in updateSupport and reset on restart.

**engineer — Runic Relics Active Collectible Subsystem:** game.runicRelic owns held/active type, duration, cooldown, nextSpawn and bounded world items. Random shield/slow runes appear at 35s, then every 45s (maximum three waiting pickups). Player proximity collects one if the held slot is empty. activateRunicRelic consumes it once for a six-second contact/gas shield or 260px 55% enemy slow field; cooldown is ten simulation seconds. No network or assets. The dedicated #runic-relic-activate button is hidden without a held/active rune, disabled when paused, in menus, active or cooling down; cooldown is shown when holding another rune. Slow/shield rings, rune glyphs, notification and synthesized cue provide feedback. A burst variant was optional and is not included.

**Integration contracts:** updateSupport combines existing Feral, rage, adrenaline and overdrive multiplicatively; beacon fire is composed before adrenaline. Example simultaneous values: speed 2.16775, damage 4, fire 1.2 (without fire beacons). Existing bounded beacon auras remain. All new timers advance only from running tick; pause/upgrades freeze them. notify accepts an optional unique event ID and uses a bounded four-entry deduplicated notification queue to avoid immediately overwriting concurrent cues. Audio occurs once at activation. Read-only diagnostics expose real buff timers, relic copies, offered choices, unlock table/availability, patch ID and last displayed notice. No production mutation/debug API was added. Existing CATACLYSM_DIAGNOSTICS, boot, game-version, controls and sound interfaces are preserved.

## Commands and evidence

- `node --check docs/preview/game.js`: PASS.
- `git diff --check`: PASS.
- `node /tmp/cataclysm-integration.cjs`: PASS. Reproducible source fixture below. It executes an in-memory instrumented copy of production code with DOM stubs; instrumentation is absent from the served game. It is not a browser/layout/audio test.
- Former-cap regression: 30 choices per tested upgrade yielded damage 8.5, speed 618.8056, shot interval .004731s, spread rank 30; every old rank/pick/HP limit crossed. Test-only repeated milestone entry inflates max HP to 370.5; that value is not a claim of a natural player's build.
- Selection tests: three enabled real choices at levels 2–99; duplicate choose calls grant only once; 100 XP resolves five consecutive menus; time remains unchanged when tick is called in upgrade mode.
- Actual production spawn function at level 999, 40 spawn attempts at each checkpoint:

| Simulation seconds | Available threats |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | shambler |
| 180 | shambler, weaver |
| 300 | shambler, weaver, dasher |
| 600 | shambler, weaver, dasher, orbiter |
| 900 | shambler, weaver, dasher, orbiter, stalker |
| 1200 | shambler, weaver, dasher, orbiter, stalker, ghost, gas |

- Every gate checked immediately before/at threshold at level 10000. Boss checked absent before 300s and present after; gas absent at 1199s, present at 1200s. Availability is measured by injected deterministic simulation state, not an observed twenty-minute human session.
- Adrenaline activation, damage reset/invulnerability exclusion, combined buff multipliers, shield escape/Overdrive expiration, rune spawn/pickup/single-use/expiration, actual shield protection from contact/gas and actual slow movement displacement: PASS.
- High-rank stress: rank 1000 spread/ricochet and .00001s shot interval remained finite, <=160 shots and <=95 enemies. An additional 120s simulated late-game sample (2400 ticks, rendering/audio stubbed) took 281ms CPU wall time locally, with peak 16 enemies and 160 shots. This is not mobile FPS or a device benchmark.
- `curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8765/preview/`: no supplied server reachable.
- `python -m http.server 8765 --directory docs`: BLOCKED, PermissionError / Operation not permitted creating server socket.
- `node game_factory/mobile_acceptance.cjs`: FAILED before any gameplay check. Chromium SIGTRAP on startup; crashpad setsockopt Operation not permitted. No 360x780 or 390x844 touch results, screenshots or browser performance results were obtained. Do not reinterpret this as acceptance passing. Runner must execute independent touch QA and game-specific portrait upgrade regressions before release.

## Limitations and following cycle

Acceptance remains blocked on actual Chromium touch checks for viewport geometry, reaching/tapping every offered button, rapid taps, focus/input restoration, simultaneous relic UI, pause/restart and mobile performance. DOM-stub tests cannot establish these. Full core-combat/audio/scoreboard regression is also awaiting browser QA. The implementation is not authorized for automatic publication by this report. Same-URL publication/live-byte verification and final release metadata stamping remain runner responsibilities outside this permitted edit scope.

Roadmap candidates deferred, not silently implemented: measured-DPS power gating with smoothing, population/threat-budget director, new environmental collisions, additional music/content proposals and a richer 1.0 encounter schedule. The supplied roadmap labels viewer proposals as unverified and says the private review was pending at its writing; no raw footage/transcript was supplied to this Coder. No direct evidence claims or fabricated player feedback are made. Existing archetypes, gas and bosses are retained and retimed; no replacement game or private evidence publication.

## Reproducible deterministic integration fixture

Save the following block as /tmp/cataclysm-integration.cjs and run `node /tmp/cataclysm-integration.cjs` from the repository root. The fixture is embedded here to respect the restriction against editing repository test files.

